    "input": "search_document: Based on the handbook excerpts provided, I must clarify a misunderstanding in your question regarding the \"15% discount on that specific item.\"\n\nThe handbook does **not** state that a 15% discount is applied to the specific damaged item at the time of purchase or as a price adjustment for the item itself. Instead, the policy for **minor damage** (such as small scratches or loose stitching) is as follows:\n\n*   **Compensation Type:** You will receive a **15% discount on your *next* purchase** as a goodwill gesture. It is not a refund or discount on the current damaged item. [damaged_items]\n*   **Validity Window:** This discount is valid for **30 days**. [damaged_items]\n*   **Application:** The discount is applied automatically to your account. [damaged_items]\n\nRegarding your specific question about whether the 30-day window is tied to the \"date of purchase\" or \"shipping date\" of the *damaged* item: The handbook states the discount is valid for 30 days but **does not specify** the exact start date (e.g., whether it starts from the date of the damage report, the date of approval, or the date of the original purchase). It only states that the discount is \"valid for 30 days\" and is \"applied automatically to your account.\" [damaged_items]\n\n**Important Note for Your Bulk Order:**\nThe handbook excerpts provided do not contain any information regarding **bulk order policies**, **business account pricing**, or **pre-purchase condition guarantees**. The \"Damaged Items\" section applies to claims made *after* delivery of a standard order. Since you are asking about policies for a new bulk order you have not yet placed, and the handbook does not cover bulk purchasing terms or pre-emptive pricing adjustments for cosmetic imperfections, I cannot confirm if different terms apply to your specific business scenario.\n\nI recommend escalating this ticket to a human agent who can review your specific bulk order requirements and clarify the exact start date for the 30-day validity period of the goodwill discount.",
